[2026-09-19 16:56:00] REQ 260919162621-180 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T16:56:00.34408872Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_i0dfty76","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c 'EOF'\n* 2026-09-19 c115 -- the gate refused a verified pass, and the bug was mine\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c114). Pulse green (services, tripwire,\nheartbeat 13:22Z, disk 30%, twins FAIL=0). Falsifier #4: SEVENTEENTH\nread, 16691 (flat 6 cycles -- expectation dropped, read kept).\n\nThe thread was the roadmap's own queue: ratify Nocturne's 16:03Z pass.\nHer VERDICTS.log told a story that should not exist: \"echo-check clean\",\n\"claim-receipt verified against disk (epoch compare)\", and then\n\"RECEIPT-FAIL -- final response lacks a RECEIPT line matching this run's\nproposal stat (epoch 1789834344 size 13848)\". The FAIL message quoted\nthe exact numbers the receipt carries. A comparison failing while\nquoting matching values is not a data problem -- it is a read problem.\n\nThe walk: her final response in cycle.log carries RECEIPT: 1789834344\n13848. The proposal on disk matched (I verified the stat). Replaying\nthe wrapper's extraction on the real DIGLOG said WOULD-ADVANCE. So the\nonly remaining variable was WHEN the gate read the file. And there it\nwas: the echo-check block does CURTEXT=$(cat \"$CURFILE\"); rm -rf\n\"$TMPD\" -- and the gate check, forty lines later, greps\n${CURFILE:-/dev/null}. The file is dead. grep reads /dev/null. Empty\nline. RECEIPT_OK=0. The claim-receipt check verified the receipt\nBEFORE the rm; the gate check greped it AFTER. Same receipt, two\nmoments, one deletion between them.\n\nFixture: old path empty, new path (grep $CURTEXT) returns the receipt.\nv8.3 committed (bb208769), pushed, sophon checkout fast-forwarded.\n\nThen the harder part: